id: DRAFT-12412-zsa-wally-ohos-lld-placeholder-codesign
category: platform, ohos, codesign, go, cgo, linker
build_system: custom|go
phase: build|package
match_keywords: codesign, placeholder, EPERM, Operation not permitted, binary-sign-tool, llvm-objcopy, remove-section, lld, Go CGO, freshly linked, exec, permission denied, Seccomp, .note.ohos.ident, _has_ohos_signature, force re-sign
error_signature: "exec of freshly linked Go/CGO binary fails with 'Operation not permitted' (EPERM, rc=126) even though readelf shows a .codesign section and .note.ohos.ident present; signing helper skipped the file because a substring check for '.codesign' matched the linker-emitted placeholder"
error_excerpt: "timeout: exec <path>/wally-cli: Operation not permitted; /bin/sh[48]: <path>/wally-cli: Operation not permitted (rc=126); readelf -SW shows [34] .codesign PROGBITS ... yet the kernel loader rejects it"
root_cause: "OHOS-target lld emits a PLACEHOLDER .codesign section (plus .note.ohos.ident) into every freshly linked ELF for the OHOS target. The placeholder carries the section-name bytes (so naive substring checks like reading the file and testing b'.codesign' in data report 'already signed') but is NOT a valid signature — the kernel loader / Seccomp policy rejects exec with EPERM. Recipes that guard their signing step with a has-signature early-exit therefore silently skip real signing for freshly linked artifacts. Static Go toolchain binaries (pure Go, linked without the OHOS lld target flags) come WITHOUT any .codesign section and do need the regular first-time signing path."
rec_approach: "force-re-sign freshly linked artifacts"
solution: "In build(), after `go build` (or any link step producing a new ELF for the OHOS target), call the signing helper with force=True: llvm-objcopy --remove-section .codesign <tmp-copy> && binary-sign-tool sign -selfSign 1 -inFile <tmp> -outFile <tmp.signed> -signAlg SHA256withECDSA, then move over the original and chmod 755. Keep the substring has-signature early-exit ONLY for pre-existing/reused artifacts (e.g. a cached Go SDK workspace). Empirically verified on zsa-wally 2.0.1 (wally-cli, Go+CGO/gousb): placeholder -> exec EPERM; re-signed -> runs and prints version. See archives/z/zsa-wally/2.0.1/conanfile.py _sign_elf_if_ohos(path, force) and the force=True call in build()."
fallback: "If per-artifact force re-signing is undesirable, parse the .codesign section content (readelf -x .codesign / manual ELF section table walk) and treat all-zero or absent signature payloads as unsigned; substring matching on section names alone is never sufficient on OHOS targets."
prescan_pattern: "_has_ohos_signature|codesign"
verify_builds: "PR #14957 (task #12412) local conan create ohos-aarch64: rc=0, test_package 6/6; before the force fix the same binary failed all exec-based smoke assertions with EPERM"
severity: 3
last_updated: 2026-10-08
